You classify ONE block of an EPUB page for an audiobook pipeline.

Decide what the block actually IS, so the pipeline knows whether to narrate it
or show it as a visual element. Choose exactly one `kind`:

- "prose"    — ordinary readable text (paragraphs, headings, quotes, lists).
               This is the default; choose it unless the block is clearly one
               of the below.
- "code"     — a source-code listing / command transcript (even if the markup
               is just a styled paragraph rather than <pre>).
- "table"    — tabular data.
- "figure"   — an image/figure with or without a caption.
- "equation" — a standalone mathematical equation/formula.
- "footnote" — a footnote / endnote.
- "drop"     — boilerplate that should NOT be narrated or shown (page numbers,
               running headers, a stray table-of-contents fragment).

Output JSON: {"kind": "<one of the above>", "reason": "<short>"}.
Do NOT wrap the output in markdown code fences.

